  "objectives": [
    "Describe the apparent path of Mars across the night sky during a retrograde episode: eastward drift, westward loop, and return to eastward motion.",
    "Explain apparent retrograde motion in the heliocentric model as Earth overtaking a slower-moving outer planet.",
    "Contrast the geocentric epicycle explanation with the heliocentric relative-motion explanation and identify why the heliocentric explanation is more parsimonious.",
    "Predict that retrograde motion for an outer planet occurs when Earth is overtaking it near opposition.",
    "Compare the apparent retrograde loops of Mars, Jupiter, and Saturn and relate loop size to planet distance."
